('ketoprofen', 'Ketoprofen', 'Ketoprofen', 'Ketoprofen', 'Ketoprofen', 'Pain & Inflammation', 'A propionic acid derivative NSAID with analgesic, anti-inflammatory and antipyretic actions, inhibiting COX enzymes and leukocyte migration.', '[''50 mg'', ''100 mg'', ''200 mg SR'', ''2.5% gel'']', '[''Capsule'', ''SR Capsule'', ''Gel'', ''Injection'']', '[''Oral'', ''Topical'', ''Intramuscular'']', 'Reversible inhibition of cyclooxygenase enzymes (COX-1 and COX-2), thereby reducing prostaglandin synthesis; also exerts mild inhibition of lipoxygenase.', 'Produces analgesia, decreases joint swelling and morning stiffness in inflammatory arthropathies.', 'Rapidly and near-completely absorbed from the GI tract; food delays peak concentration but not extent of absorption.', 'High volume into synovial fluid; 99% bound to plasma proteins (predominantly albumin).', 'Extensive hepatic glucuronidation to inactive glucuronide conjugates.', 'Approximately 80% eliminated in urine, largely as glucuronide conjugates.', 'Approximately 90%', '1.5 to 2 hours (immediate release); prolonged in sustained-release forms', 'Approximately 99%', '30 to 60 minutes orally', '4 to 6 hours (standard); up to 24 hours (SR)', '[''Rheumatoid arthritis'', ''Osteoarthritis'', ''Acute musculoskeletal pain'', ''Dysmenorrhoea'', ''Ankylosing spondylitis'']', '[''Active peptic ulceration or GI bleeding'', ''Severe renal or hepatic failure'', ''Severe heart failure'', ''History of aspirin/NSAID-induced asthma or urticaria'']', '[''Risk of GI ulceration and bleeding'', ''Fluid retention and cardiovascular thrombotic risk'', ''Renal papillary necrosis with prolonged use'']', '[''Dyspepsia'', ''Nausea'', ''Abdominal discomfort'', ''Headache'', ''Dizziness'']', '[''Gastrointestinal haemorrhage'', ''Acute kidney injury'', ''Bronchospasm in aspirin-sensitive asthmatics'', ''Photosensitivity reactions'']', '[''Anticoagulants (increased bleeding risk)'', ''ACE inhibitors and diuretics (reduced antihypertensive effect, 