('cefazolin', 'Cefazolin', 'Cefazolin', 'Cefazolin sodium', 'Cefazolin sodium', 'Antibiotics', 'A first-generation parenteral cephalosporin with excellent activity against MSSA and Streptococcus, established worldwide as the gold standard for surgical antibiotic prophylaxis.', '[''500 mg'', ''1 g'', ''2 g vial'']', '[''Powder for Injection'']', '[''Intravenous'', ''Intramuscular'']', 'Binds to bacterial penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs), inhibiting cross-linking of peptidoglycan in the cell wall, causing cell lysis.', 'High bactericidal activity against methicillin-sensitive Staphylococcus aureus (MSSA), Streptococcus pyogenes, and select community Gram-negatives (E. coli, Proteus mirabilis).', '100% bioavailable IV; rapid and complete absorption after IM injection.', 'Widely distributed into bone, synovial fluid, pleural fluid, and surgical wound tissue; 80-85% bound to plasma proteins.', 'Not metabolized in the liver; excreted unchanged.', 'Approximately 80-100% eliminated unchanged in urine via glomerular filtration and tubular secretion.', '100% (IV)', '1.8 to 2 hours', '80% to 85%', 'Immediate (IV); peak tissue levels within 30 minutes', '6 to 8 hours', '[''Surgical antibiotic prophylaxis (clean and clean-contaminated procedures)'', ''Methicillin-susceptible Staphylococcus aureus (MSSA) bacteremia and endocarditis'', ''Complicated skin and skin structure infections'', ''Bone and joint infections (osteomyelitis, septic arthritis)'']', '[''Hypersensitivity to cefazolin, cephalosporins, or severe immediate beta-lactam anaphylaxis'']', '[''Infuse within 60 minutes prior to surgical incision for optimal tissue protection'', ''Dose adjustment in renal failure'', ''Clostridioides difficile colitis'']', '[''Phlebitis'', ''Diarrhoea'', ''Transient elevation of liver transaminases'', ''Rash'', ''Nausea'']', '[''Pseudomembranous colitis'', ''Anaphylaxis'', ''Neutropenia (prolonged therapy)'', ''Seizures in high-dose renal impairment'']', '[''Probenecid (prolongs cefazoli