('cefditoren', 'Cefditoren', 'Cefditoren Pivoxil', 'Cefditoren pivoxil', 'Cefditoren pivoxil', 'Antibiotics', 'An oral third-generation cephalosporin prodrug with enhanced affinity for penicillin-resistant Streptococcus pneumoniae and common respiratory pathogens.', '[''200 mg'', ''400 mg'']', '[''Film-coated Tablet'']', '[''Oral'']', 'Hydrolyzed by esterases during absorption to active cefditoren, which binds to PBPs and inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis.', 'High bactericidal activity against Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella catarrhalis, and MSSA.', 'Bioavailability approximately 14% on empty stomach, significantly increased when taken with a high-fat meal.', 'Good penetration into tonsillar tissue, bronchial mucosa, and middle ear fluid; 88% bound to plasma proteins.', 'Prodrug pivoxil moiety cleaved by intestinal esterases to active cefditoren and pivalate; pivalate is conjugated with carnitine and excreted.', 'Eliminated primarily unchanged by the kidneys in urine via glomerular filtration and tubular secretion.', '14% fasting, up to 20% with high-fat meals', '1.6 hours', '88%', '1.5 to 3 hours', '12 hours', '[''Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis'', ''Community-acquired pneumonia'', ''Pharyngitis / tonsillitis'', ''Uncomplicated skin and skin structure infections'']', '[''Hypersensitivity to cephalosporins or beta-lactams'', ''Carnitine deficiency or inborn errors of metabolism causing carnitine loss'', ''Known milk protein hypersensitivity (contains sodium caseinate)'']', '[''Carnitine depletion with prolonged therapy (pivalate conjugates carnitine)'', ''Must take with meals to maximize absorption'', ''Pseudomembranous colitis'']', '[''Diarrhoea'', ''Nausea'', ''Headache'', ''Abdominal pain'', ''Dyspepsia'']', '[''Carnitine deficiency syndrome'', ''Clostridioides difficile colitis'', ''Anaphylaxis'', ''Severe cutaneous adverse reactions'']', '[''Antacids and H2-blockers (decrease oral absorption)'', ''Probenecid (increases