('ampicillin-sulbactam', 'Ampicillin / Sulbactam', 'Ampicillin + Sulbactam', 'Ampicillin sodium and sulbactam sodium', 'Ampicillin sodium and sulbactam sodium', 'Antibiotics', 'An injectable aminopenicillin combined with a beta-lactamase inhibitor, providing broad coverage against beta-lactamase producing organisms, anaerobes, and Acinetobacter baumannii.', '[''750 mg'', ''1.5 g'', ''3 g vial'']', '[''Powder for Injection'']', '[''Intravenous'', ''Intramuscular'']', 'Ampicillin inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis; sulbactam irreversibly binds and inactivates beta-lactamases and has intrinsic bactericidal activity against Acinetobacter baumannii PBPs.', 'Bactericidal against MSSA, Streptococcus, Enterococcus faecalis, Listeria, anaerobes (Bacteroides fragilis), and Acinetobacter baumannii.', '100% bioavailable upon intravenous administration; well absorbed intramuscularly.', 'Widely distributed in peritoneal fluid, skin blister fluid, lung, and bile; 28% (ampicillin) and 38% (sulbactam) protein bound.', 'Minimal hepatic metabolism; both drugs eliminated largely unchanged.', 'Approximately 75-85% of both ampicillin and sulbactam eliminated unchanged in urine within 8 hours.', '100% (IV)', '1 hour (parent drug and inhibitor have parallel kinetics)', '28% to 38%', 'Immediate (IV)', '6 to 8 hours', '[''Acinetobacter baumannii hospital-acquired infections and ventilator pneumonia (high-dose sulbactam regimens)'', ''Intra-abdominal infections (appendicitis, peritonitis)'', ''Gynecological infections / pelvic inflammatory disease'', ''Diabetic foot infections (polymicrobial coverage)'', ''Aspiration pneumonia and lung abscess'']', '[''Hypersensitivity to ampicillin, sulbactam, or penicillins'', ''History of cholestatic jaundice / hepatic dysfunction associated with ampicillin-sulbactam'']', '[''Severe anaphylactic reactions in penicillin-allergic patients'', ''Clostridioides difficile colitis'', ''Renal dose adjustment essential'']', '[''Pain at injection site'', ''Diarr