('ceftolozane-tazobactam', 'Ceftolozane / Tazobactam', 'Ceftolozane + Tazobactam', 'Ceftolozane sulfate and tazobactam sodium', 'Ceftolozane sulfate and tazobactam sodium', 'Antibiotics', 'An advanced antipseudomonal cephalosporin combined with a beta-lactamase inhibitor, engineered specifically to overcome multidrug-resistant Pseudomonas aeruginosa.', '[''1.5 g vial (1 g ceftolozane / 0.5 g tazobactam)'', ''3 g vial (2 g ceftolozane / 1 g tazobactam)'']', '[''Powder for Concentrate for Solution for Infusion'']', '[''Intravenous'']', 'Ceftolozane inhibits PBPs (PBP1b, PBP1c, PBP3) with high affinity and resistance to ampC hydrolysis and efflux pumps; tazobactam protects against most class A and class C beta-lactamases.', 'Unrivalled bactericidal activity against multidrug-resistant and extensively drug-resistant (MDR/XDR) Pseudomonas aeruginosa and ESBL-producing Enterobacteriaceae.', '100% bioavailable by IV infusion over 1 hour.', 'Good penetration into pulmonary epithelial lining fluid and abdominal tissues; 16-21% (ceftolozane) and 30% (tazobactam) protein bound.', 'Minimal hepatic metabolism; ceftolozane not metabolized by CYP enzymes.', 'Over 95% of ceftolozane and 80% of tazobactam eliminated unchanged in urine via glomerular filtration.', '100% (IV)', '2.7 to 3 hours', '16% to 21%', 'Immediate upon IV infusion', '8 hours', '[''Hospital-acquired bacterial pneumonia and ventilator-associated pneumonia (HABP/VABP)'', ''Complicated intra-abdominal infections (combined with metronidazole)'', ''Complicated urinary tract infections including acute pyelonephritis'', ''Multidrug-resistant (MDR) Pseudomonas aeruginosa sepsis'']', '[''Severe hypersensitivity to ceftolozane, tazobactam, or other beta-lactams'']', '[''Renal dose adjustment is critical (higher failure rates if underdosed in moderate renal impairment)'', ''Pseudomembranous colitis'', ''Direct Coombs test seroconversion'']', '[''Nausea'', ''Diarrhoea'', ''Headache'', ''Pyrexia'', ''Constipation'']', '[''Clo