('luliconazole', 'Luliconazole', 'Luliconazole', 'Luliconazole', 'Luliconazole', 'Antifungals', 'A potent topical imidazole antifungal with exceptionally low minimum inhibitory concentrations (MICs) against dermatophytes, permitting once-daily application for only 1 to 2 weeks.', '[''1% cream'', ''1% lotion'']', '[''Topical Cream'', ''Topical Lotion'']', '[''Topical'']', 'Inhibits fungal lanosterol 14-alpha-demethylase, disrupting ergosterol synthesis in fungal cell membranes; uniquely incorporates an optically active R-enantiomer dithioacetal structure providing extreme affinity for dermatophyte enzymes.', 'Broad fungicidal activity against Trichophyton rubrum, Trichophyton mentagrophytes, Epidermophyton floccosum, and Malassezia; MIC values are significantly lower than terbinafine, clotrimazole, and ketoconazole.', 'Minimal systemic absorption after topical application; concentrates heavily in the stratum corneum with sustained reservoirs.', 'High retention in keratinized skin layers; systemic plasma concentrations remain negligible (<5 ng/mL).', 'Any absorbed drug is metabolized in the liver via glucuronidation and CYP pathways.', 'Excreted in urine and faeces as trace inactive metabolites.', '<1% systemic bioavailability', '24 to 36 hours retention in stratum corneum', '>99% systemically', 'Rapid relief of pruritus and scaling within 3 to 5 days', '24 hours (once-daily application)', '[''Tinea cruris (jock itch)'', ''Tinea corporis (ringworm)'', "Tinea pedis (athlete''s foot - interdigital and plantaris)"]', '[''Hypersensitivity to luliconazole or any component of the cream/lotion'', ''Ophthalmic, oral, or intravaginal use'']', '[''For external topical dermatological use only; avoid contact with eyes and mucous membranes'', ''Contact dermatitis and local allergic sensitization'']', '[''Application site pruritus'', ''Mild local skin burning sensation'', ''Contact dermatitis'', ''Erythema'']', '[''Severe allergic contact dermatitis / blistering (rare)'', ''Seconda