('tolfenamic-acid', 'Tolfenamic acid', 'Tolfenamic acid', 'Tolfenamic acid', 'Tolfenamic acid', 'Pain & Inflammation', 'An anthranilic acid derivative (fenamate) NSAID used extensively for the acute abortive treatment of migraine attacks and inflammatory joint disorders.', '[''100 mg'', ''200 mg'']', '[''Tablet'', ''Capsule'']', '[''Oral'']', 'Inhibits cyclooxygenase (COX) enzymes to reduce prostaglandin synthesis, and uniquely exerts direct antagonist actions at prostaglandin receptor sites.', 'Relieves acute migraine headache, nausea, and photophobia by attenuating neurogenic vascular inflammation and prostaglandin-mediated cranial vasodilation.', 'Rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract; peak plasma concentrations achieved in 1 to 2 hours.', 'Extensively bound to plasma proteins (>99%); crosses blood-brain barrier effectively to act on cranial vasculature.', 'Metabolized extensively in the liver by oxidation, hydroxylation, and glucuronide conjugation.', 'Approximately 90% eliminated in urine (mainly as metabolites) and remainder via faeces.', 'Approximately 75-80%', '2 to 3 hours', '>99%', '30 to 45 minutes', '6 to 8 hours', '[''Acute migraine attacks (abortive treatment)'', ''Tension headache'', ''Rheumatoid arthritis'', ''Dysmenorrhoea'', ''Post-extraction dental pain'']', '[''Active gastrointestinal bleeding or ulcer'', ''Severe renal or hepatic failure'', ''Aspirin-sensitive asthma'', ''Third trimester of pregnancy'']', '[''Take at the earliest sign of migraine aura or attack for maximal efficacy'', ''GI bleeding risk'', ''Renal hemodynamic compromise'']', '[''Dyspepsia'', ''Diarrhoea'', ''Nausea'', ''Dizziness'', ''Dysuria / mild urinary burning (characteristic of fenamates)'']', '[''Gastrointestinal ulceration'', ''Haemolytic anaemia (rare with fenamates)'', ''Bronchospasm'']', '[''Anticoagulants'', ''Lithium'', ''Methotrexate'', ''Antihypertensives'', ''Other NSAIDs'']', '[''Migraine frequency and relief'', ''Renal function'', ''Complete blood counts during chronic use'']', 'Contraindicated in third trimester; avoid in pregnancy unless directed by specialist.', 'Excreted in low levels in breast milk; use caution.', 'Not recommended in children for migraine.', 'Reduced renal reserve requires careful monitoring; use lowest effective dose.', 'Avoid in severe renal impairment; monitor hydration.', 'Reduce dose in moderate hepatic disease; contraindicated in severe hepatic failure.', '[''Direct prostaglandin receptor antagonism enhances anti-migraine efficacy'', ''Rapid absorption ideal for aborting headache flares'']', '[''Can cause mild urinary irritation / dysuria in some individuals'', ''Short half-life may require second dose if attack recurs'']', '[''Take at the first warning signs of migraine'', ''Dual action: blocks prostaglandin synthesis AND receptor binding'']', 'TOL-fenamic: TOLerates migraine NO MORE.', '-fenamic acid', 'tol-fe-NAM-ik AS-id', 'टॉलफेनामिक एसिड', 'active', 'verified', NULL, NULL),
