('tizanidine', 'Tizanidine', 'Tizanidine', 'Tizanidine hydrochloride', 'Tizanidine hydrochloride', 'Pain & Inflammation', 'A centrally acting alpha-2 adrenergic agonist that reduces muscle spasticity by promoting presynaptic inhibition of motor neurons, with minimal muscle weakness.', '[''2 mg'', ''4 mg'', ''6 mg'']', '[''Tablet'', ''Capsule'']', '[''Oral'']', 'Selective agonist at central presynaptic alpha-2 adrenergic receptors; decreases the release of excitatory amino acids from spinal interneurons.', 'Reduces muscle tone and frequency of painful spasms without significantly diminishing voluntary muscle strength, unlike baclofen.', 'Rapidly and near-completely absorbed; undergoes substantial hepatic first-pass metabolism.', 'Apparent volume of distribution 2.4 L/kg; 30% bound to plasma proteins.', 'Extensively metabolized by cytochrome P450 1A2 (CYP1A2) to inactive metabolites.', 'Approximately 60% recovered in urine and 20% in faeces as inactive metabolites.', 'Approximately 34-40% due to first-pass metabolism', '2.5 hours', '30%', '1 to 2 hours', '3 to 6 hours', '[''Spasticity associated with multiple sclerosis or spinal cord injury'', ''Painful acute musculoskeletal spasm'', ''Cervical dystonia / tension headache (adjunctive)'']', '[''Concomitant use of potent CYP1A2 inhibitors (ciprofloxacin, fluvoxamine) - leads to severe hypotension and somnolence'', ''Severe hepatic impairment'']', '[''Hypotension and bradycardia (alpha-2 agonist hemodynamic effects)'', ''Sedation and dizziness'', ''Hepatotoxicity: monitor liver enzymes'']', '[''Dry mouth'', ''Somnolence'', ''Dizziness'', ''Fatigue'', ''Asthenia'']', '[''Severe symptomatic hypotension / syncope'', ''Drug-induced liver injury (ALT/AST elevation)'', ''Hallucinations'', ''QT prolongation'']', '[''Ciprofloxacin and fluvoxamine (contraindicated; marked increase in tizanidine exposure)'', ''Oral contraceptives (inhibit CYP1A2)'', ''Antihypertensives (additive hypotension)'', ''Alcohol and CNS depressants'']', '