('tolperisone', 'Tolperisone', 'Tolperisone', 'Tolperisone hydrochloride', 'Tolperisone hydrochloride', 'Pain & Inflammation', 'A centrally acting muscle relaxant with membrane-stabilizing and sodium-channel blocking actions that reduces muscle spasticity and tone without significant sedation.', '[''50 mg'', ''150 mg'', ''450 mg SR'']', '[''Film-coated Tablet'', ''Sustained-Release Tablet'']', '[''Oral'']', 'Inhibits voltage-gated sodium channels, stabilizing neuronal membranes; depresses mono- and polysynaptic spinal cord reflex pathways and reticulospinal tract transmission.', 'Reduces muscular hypertonia and reflex spasms while preserving psychomotor performance and alertness, unlike conventional sedating muscle relaxants.', 'Well absorbed from the GI tract; peak plasma concentrations attained in 0.5 to 1.5 hours.', 'Widely distributed into tissues; 80% protein bound.', 'Extensively metabolised in the liver and kidneys, primarily via CYP2D6 and CYP2C19.', 'Greater than 99% eliminated via renal excretion as inactive metabolites.', 'Approximately 17-20% due to high first-pass effect; enhanced when taken with meals.', '1.5 to 2.5 hours', '80%', '30 to 60 minutes', '4 to 6 hours (standard); up to 12-24 hours (SR)', '[''Post-stroke spasticity in adults'', ''Acute painful muscle contractures and spinal spasticity'', ''Lumbago and cervical spine disorders'']', '[''Myasthenia gravis'', ''Hypersensitivity to tolperisone'', ''Lactation'']', '[''Hypersensitivity reactions ranging from mild skin rash to severe anaphylaxis'', ''Take after meals to enhance oral bioavailability'']', '[''Dyspepsia'', ''Nausea'', ''Dry mouth'', ''Headache'', ''Muscle weakness'']', '[''Anaphylactic shock'', ''Angioedema'', ''Bronchospasm'']', '[''Substrates of CYP2D6 (may increase levels of thioridazine, tolterodine, venlafaxine)'', ''Other centrally acting muscle relaxants'']', '[''Signs of hypersensitivity or cutaneous reactions'', ''Relief of spasticity and motor function'']', 'Avoid during pre